1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,200
This philosophy would be embodied in what need would term the uber mench or overman or sometimes translated as the superman.
这种哲学体现在视频所说的“超人”概念中，英语有 overman 或 superman 等译法；原字幕术语识别待核。

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,160
Which he would first introduce in his book thus spoke zaratustra.
视频说，他首次在《查拉图斯特拉如是说》中引入这一概念；书名识别待核。

3
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:21,560
The overman is described as a sort of defiant confident independent individual who pursues their personal desires with vigor and dignifies their independent beliefs unapologetically.
超人被描绘为反抗、坚定、独立的人，积极追求个人欲望，毫不歉疚地维护自己的信念，

4
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:28,079
One who deviates from the collective exhibits strategic selfishness and acts with aggressiveness and grandiose.
偏离群体，展现策略性的自利，并带有进取和宏大姿态；grandiose 原词形待核。

5
00:00:28,079 --> 00:00:38,160
The reason for such characteristics was justified in n's view by the fact that a new morality that opposed the moral views rooted in christianity which praised weakness and modesty.
叙述者说，在尼采看来，这些特质的理由是需要一种与基督教道德相对的新道德，后者在该叙述中推崇柔弱与谦逊，

6
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:48,280
Was needed to better suit the natural condition of human experience which he felt was comprised and requiring of the desire for vigor power and greatness.
以更适合他认为包含、也需要活力、力量与卓越欲望的人类处境。

7
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:52,679
This view is not without valid critiques and invalid misinterpretations.
这种观点既受到合理批评，也遭遇不当误读。

8
00:00:52,679 --> 00:01:00,200
However perhaps what is more important than n's image of the overman is what the concept serves to represent in slightly broader terms.
不过，也许更重要的不是“超人”的形象，而是这个概念在更广泛层面代表了什么。

9
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:05,079
Nche sets up the overman to function as a sort of idealized version of oneself.
叙述者说，超人发挥着一种理想化自我的作用。

10
00:01:05,079 --> 00:01:13,600
An image of a perfect and powerful being who has overcome all their fears and deficiencies which one can and should set goals to strive towards.
它是克服了所有恐惧与缺陷的完美强大形象，人可以朝它设定目标、努力前进。

11
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:19,320
Of course as an ideal it cannot ever truly be reached but that is functionally the point.
当然，既然是理想，它永远无法真正达到，但作者说，这正是它发挥作用的方式。

12
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:24,760
N proposed that the world including the human operates off of what he called the will to power.
叙述者说，尼采提出世界，包括人，是按照他所谓的“权力意志”运作的。

13
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:28,920
An insatiable desire in each living being to manifest power.
它是每种生命中展现力量的、无法满足的欲望。

14
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:32,480
The world is will to power and nothing besides he wrote.
视频引述：“世界是权力意志，除此之外别无他物。”

15
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:40,480
And according to n this will to power is manifested in the desire for personal growth and satisfied in the pursuance of said growth.
按照视频对尼采的解读，这种意志体现在个人成长的欲望中，并在追求成长时得到满足。

16
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:46,079
It is important to note here that his notion of power is not necessarily referring to physical strength.
这里需要指出，他所谓的力量未必指身体强健，

17
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:51,119
Nor power in dominance over others but rather power over oneself.
也不是支配他人的权力，而是对自己的掌控。

18
00:01:51,119 --> 00:01:59,560
Psychological and spiritual strength in the form of self mastery and continuous growth represents the ultimate synchronization with the will to power for n.
以自我掌握和持续成长为形式的心理与精神力量，在该解读中代表与权力意志的高度一致，

19
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:02,959
And thus the ultimate synchronization with life itself.
因而也就是与生命本身的一致。

20
00:02:02,959 --> 00:02:09,000
The desire and striving towards the ideal of the overman serves as perpetual fuel to this process of self growth.
向超人理想努力的愿望，为这种自我成长的过程提供不断的动力，

21
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:17,000
As one works through a continued cycle of self dissatisfaction self improvement and self rediscovery over and over.
人在其中反复经历自我不满、自我改善和重新认识自己的循环。

22
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:25,320
Forn this process which he would term self overcoming is fundamental to answering and resolving the problem of meaning and value in life.
在视频解读中，这个被称为“自我超越”的过程，是回答生命意义和价值问题的基础。

23
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:32,560
So long as one establishes their goals of growth in the name of what they deem an idealized life affirming version of them themselves.
前提是，人把成长目标设在自己认定的、肯定生命的理想自我方向上；保留字幕自我修正。

24
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:38,120
The process transmutes the suffering of life into something worthwhile and personally redeemable.
叙述者说，这个过程把生活中的痛苦转化为值得、也对个人有救赎意义的东西，

25
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:43,159
A sort of alchemy of the spirit that affirms life in the face of its inevitable suffering.
像一种精神的炼金术，即便面对不可避免的痛苦，仍然肯定生命。

26
00:02:43,159 --> 00:02:48,960
If we have our own why in life we shall get along with almost any how n wrote.
视频引述：如果人有自己的“为何”，就能应对几乎任何“如何”。

27
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:56,240
Unlike his primary predecessor arthur schopenhauer who proposed that suffering is best minimized and avoided to the best of one's ability.
视频将之与叔本华对比，说后者主张尽可能减少并避免痛苦。

28
00:02:56,240 --> 00:03:06,080
N argued that suffering is rather a good thing to be leaned into embraced and used as fuel towards the amassing of strength and psychological power.
而视频说，尼采把痛苦看作可迎向、接纳并用来积累力量的东西；这是观点转述，不是健康指导。

29
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:11,800
Life is in fact inevitable suffering and so it is not a matter of if but for what.
作者继续说，人生难免痛苦，所以问题不是会不会，而是为了什么。

30
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:20,279
The meaninglessness of suffering not suffering itself was the curse that lay over mankind so far n wrote.
视频引述：迄今笼罩人类的诅咒，是痛苦没有意义，而非痛苦本身。
